The bird is launched from the left and follows a parabolic trajectory under gravity. In the first frame (t=0.00), it is near pig 1. By t=0.13, it has moved past pig 1 and is approaching pig 2. By t=0.27, it is above pig 2 and heading toward pig 3. By t=0.37, it is just above pig 3.

Since the bird is still in the air and moving toward pig 3, it will hit pig 3. The bird will hit pig 3 with enough force to kill it. After the bird hits pig 3, the bird will continue flying and eventually fall out of the frame, as no other objects are in its path. Pigs 1 and 2 are not hit by the bird and remain undisturbed. The structures (the brown blocks and the table) are not hit by the bird, so they remain intact. Therefore, pigs 1 and 2 survive.

